    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Dorrian are delighted to present to the market this beautifully renovated two-bedroom cottage, enjoying an exceptional position on the breathtaking coastal retreat of Cruit Island, Kincasslagh. Set within one of Donegal's most scenic and unspoilt coastal locations, the property is surrounded by pristine sandy beaches, rugged shoreline walks, and crystal-clear Atlantic waters, creating a truly idyllic escape for those seeking peace, privacy, and natural beauty along the Wild Atlantic coastline.\n\nPresented in excellent turn-key condition, the cottage was carefully renovated and remodelled by the current owner in 2016, resulting in a charming and comfortable home that successfully blends traditional coastal character with modern convenience. Its bright, well-appointed accommodation is ideally suited as a holiday home, weekend retreat, investment opportunity, or permanent residence for those wishing to embrace a slower pace of life in a spectacular seaside setting. Cruit Island Golf\nClub is located less than a ten-minute walk away, further enhancing the lifestyle appeal of this delightful property in one of West Donegal's most desirable coastal locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nStorm Porch: - 2.3m x 1.7m\n wall-to-wall glazing with fitted roller blinds, feature white oak vaulted ceiling, glass centre light, uPVC door with clear glass panel, radiator with TRV valve, open arch to the inner hall, and stone-effect ceramic floor tiles.\n\nInner Hall: - 2.6m x 1.3m\nstone-effect ceramic tiled floor, pull-down stairs to a fully floored attic providing good storage space, and centre light.\n\nSitting Room: - 3.9m x 3.2m\n light oak-effect laminate floor, feature red brick fireplace with built-in “Olymberyl” cast iron stove serving 12 radiators, overhead downlighters, coaxial TV wall socket, exposed ceiling beams, inset ceiling lights, and frosted glass centre light with matching wall lights.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: - 4.5m x 3.9m\n country-style kitchen with oak-effect worktops, built-in “Zanussi” electric oven, four-ring induction hob, wooden extractor canopy, integrated “Zanussi” dishwasher, fridge/freezer, fitted washing machine, one-and-a-half stainless steel sink with swan-neck mixer tap, stone-effect cladded splashback, three glass display cabinets with downlighters and tempered glass shelves, inset ceiling lights, fitted corner dresser, oak-effect ceramic tiled floor, dual-aspect windows, rear door with frosted glass panel, two-zone central heating timer, and hotpress with factory-insulated tank.\n\nBathroom: - 2.0m x 1.5m\n modern white sanitary ware comprising a six-jet jacuzzi bath with chrome shower cradle and Triton electric shower, pedestal wash hand basin, tempered glass shelf with mirror over, dual-flush WC, inset lights, full tiling, radiator, and folding shower screen.\n\nBedroom 1: - 2.6m x 2.5m\n built-in wall-to-wall wardrobes around the bed, pine tongue-and- groove ceiling panelling, centre light, east-facing window, radiator with thermostatic control, and downlighters above the bed.\n\nEn-suite: - 2.7m x 0.9m\n modern white sanitary ware comprising a dual-flush WC, built-in vanity basin with mixer tap and inset lights over, fully tiled shower cubicle with tempered glass door, “Triton TS 2000xr” electric shower, frosted glass centre light, tiled floor, ceiling coving, and oak-effect laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom 2: - 2.8m x 2.7m\n built-in wall-to-wall wardrobes around the bed, pine tongue-and- groove ceiling panelling, centre light, east-facing window, radiator with thermostatic control, and downlighters above the bed and windowsill.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Additional Features:</li><li> Instantly appealing two-bedroom cottage extending to circa 75.8 sq.m / 815 sq.ft in area, set on a site of approximately 0.65 acres.</li><li> Positioned within one of Donegal's most scenic and desirable coastal settings.</li><li> Surrounded by beautiful sandy beaches, rugged shoreline walks, and crystal-clear Atlantic waters.</li><li> Ideally suited as a holiday home, coastal retreat, or permanent residence.</li><li> Front garden laid in lawn, tarmacked driveway with ample parking to rear.</li><li> Presented in excellent turn-key condition throughout with all furniture included in the sale.</li><li> Painstakingly renovated and remodelled by the current owner in 2016.</li><li> Comfortable, well-appointed accommodation with charming coastal character.</li><li> Welcoming storm porch with wall-to-wall glazing, vaulted white oak ceiling, and stone-effect tiled flooring.</li><li> Cosy sitting room featuring exposed ceiling beams, red brick fireplace, and built-in Olymberyl cast iron stove serving 12 radiators.</li><li> Attractive country-style kitchen/dining room with oak-effect worktops, integrated appliances, display cabinets, fitted dresser, and dual-aspect windows.</li><li> Modern fully tiled bathroom with six-jet jacuzzi bath and Triton electric shower.</li><li> Two bedrooms, both fitted with wall-to-wall built-in wardrobes and pine tongue-and-groove ceiling panelling.</li><li> Principal bedroom benefits from an en-suite shower room with modern white sanitary ware and Triton electric shower.</li><li> Pull-down stairs to a fully floored attic, providing useful additional storage space.</li><li> Oil-fired central heating supported by stove heating system serving 12 radiators.</li><li> Cruit Island Golf Club is located less than a ten-minute walk away.</li><li> Excellent lifestyle appeal in one of West Donegal's most sought-after seaside locations.</li><li> Viewings by prior arrangement with DNG Dorrian on 074 97 31291</ul>"
      },
